From: Christopher Parris <parricc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmd: Prime the console input path before waiting in WCMD_wait_for_input().

WCMD_wait_for_input() waits on the console input handle before it has issued
any read, which deadlocks on a Unix console. "wine cmd /c pause" therefore
hangs forever in a terminal and no keypress will release it.

On a Unix console the console input object cannot become signaled until
conhost's tty_input() thread is reading the terminal. That thread is started
only by ensure_tty_input_thread(), which is reached only from the six
read/peek ioctls in console_input_ioctl() -- IOCTL_CONDRV_READ_CONSOLE,
READ_CONSOLE_CONTROL, READ_FILE, READ_INPUT, PEEK and GET_INPUT_INFO. The
main() call site is guarded by !console->is_unix, so it does not apply here.

In this function the only call that issues one of those ioctls is
has_pending_char_events(), via GetNumberOfConsoleInputEvents(), and it sits
inside the loop body after the wait. So the wait needs input records, the
records need the reader thread, and the reader thread needs a read that only
happens once the wait has already returned. Nothing starts, and because
ensure_tty_input_thread() returns TRUE when console->tty_input is NULL and
its return value is discarded at all six call sites, nothing is logged
either.

Calling has_pending_char_events() once before the loop starts the reader and
lets the subsequent wait behave normally. The result is assigned to
return_code rather than returned directly so that the SetConsoleMode() restore
at the end of the function still runs.

Reproduced identically on macOS 26.5.1 (arm64, x86_64 Wine under Rosetta) and
on Linux with a Flatpak build reporting wine-11.0, so this is not
platform-specific. WCMD_wait_for_input() is unchanged between wine-11.0 and
current master.

Distinguishing observation: typing "pause" at an interactive "wine cmd" prompt
works correctly, because reading the command line has already started the
reader thread. Only the non-interactive "cmd /c pause" hangs. "dir /p" hangs
the same way once the listing is long enough to page.
---
 programs/cmd/wcmdmain.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/programs/cmd/wcmdmain.c
+++ b/programs/cmd/wcmdmain.c
@@ -617,6 +617,14 @@ RETURN_CODE WCMD_wait_for_input(HANDLE hIn)
     {
         SetConsoleMode(hIn, oldmode & ~ENABLE_LINE_INPUT);
         FlushConsoleInputBuffer(hIn);
+        /* On a Unix console the input object cannot become signaled until
+         * conhost's tty reader thread is running, and that thread is only
+         * started by a read or peek ioctl.  Prime the input path here so the
+         * wait below can be satisfied: has_pending_char_events() issues
+         * GetNumberOfConsoleInputEvents(), which is enough to start it.
+         * Assigned rather than returned so the mode restore still runs. */
+        if (has_pending_char_events(hIn))
+            return_code = NO_ERROR;
         while (return_code == ERROR_SIGNAL_PENDING)
         {
             switch (WaitForMultipleObjects(2, h, FALSE, INFINITE))
